d asked Jolene for strategies used.\n  - routines: Jolene is seeking new routines. Deborah suggested a gentle yoga flow focused on breathing and grounding to help Jolene cope, and offered to send a tutorial video.\n  - planners: Jolene started using a bullet journal to track tasks and stay organized as part of her time management strategies.\n  - studying: Jolene has a schedule that includes studying, classes, and personal time, using yoga and meditation for balance.\n  - tips: Deborah offered tips to Jolene for yoga practice, and Jolene thanked her and said she would check them out.\n  - time for myself: Jolene uses breathing, meditation, and yoga to feel calmer, clearer, more alert, and motivated, and continues taking time for herself with Deborah's support.\n  - organization: No specific organization was mentioned in the conversation between Jolene and Deborah, which focused on stress, exams, deadlines, and time management.\n  - studies: Jolene uses meditation to help her stay balanced during her studies.\n  - schedule: Jolene plans to check her schedule next month to arrange a time to chat with Deborah.\n  - Jolene and Anna: Deborah mentioned Anna got her a tasty vegan stir-fry (tofu, veg, ginger, soy sauce). Jolene mentioned doing yoga and meditation last Friday for me-time.\n  - things that bring you joy: Deborah advises Jolene to make time for 'things that bring you joy' to experience joy.\n  - time management: Jolene struggles with balancing engineering, relationship, and personal growth, and is now using a bullet journal for time management.\n  - example from last Friday: Jolene mentioned an overwhelming stack of tasks, providing an example from last Friday, after discussing time management difficulties.\n  - planner: Deborah suggested using planners or schedulers for time management to ensure time for oneself.\n  - tracks: Jolene asked Deb about any favorite music tracks.\n  - \"It takes two\": \"It takes two\" is a fun, competitive team-strategy game Jolene and another person (implied) enjoy playing together to bond.\n  - routine: Jolene finds having a routine helpful for classes, studying, and personal time, including self-care like yoga and meditation for balance. Surroundings can affect mood and zen gained from the routine.\n  - mindfulness: Jolene realized the importance of mindfulness, self-care, and balance alongside engineering studies after a meditation retreat in Phuket. Deborah encourages this practice.\n  - visualization: Jolene found the shared visualization helpful.\n  - Engineering assignments: Jolene is struggling to manage her Engineering assignments and is asking to discuss time management.\n  - deadlines: Deborah expressed concern to Jolene about her exams and deadlines, noting the situation is difficult. Jolene confirmed it is tough, stressful, and requires her to constantly play catch-up.\n  - stack of tasks: Jolene finds a large stack of tasks overwhelming, even after trying to make a list for time management.\n  - personal time: Jolene schedules personal time as part of her routine to stay balanced and relax, alongside classes and studying.\n  - chill time: Jolene expressed a strong desire for chill time after Deborah mentioned a peaceful yoga retreat.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2003,"context_chars":8136,"retrieval_duration":0.4204220771789551,"response_duration":2.172046661376953,"total_duration":2.592468738555908,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer includes the key elements of breaking tasks into smaller pieces, setting goals, and making a schedule, which aligns with the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all necessary information to answer the question regarding what Jolene and Deb discussed as helpful strategies for studying and time management. Specifically, it mentions breaking tasks into smaller pieces and setting goals, as well as using planners or schedulers, which are the key elements outlined in the golden answer.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["breaking tasks into smaller pieces","setting goals","using planners or schedulers"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_8","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_8_qa_153","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What did Evan share a photo of that was taken on a camping trip?","golden_answer":"a kayak","hypothesis":"Evan shared a photo of an amazing sunset that was taken during a camping trip on July 1, 2023.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Evan took a picture during a camping trip (event_time: 2023-07-01T00:00:00Z)\n  - Evan's picture or memory discussed originated from a trip to Banff. (event_time: 2023-12-09T13:45:00Z)\n  - Evan took a picture of an amazing sunset (event_time: 2023-07-01T00:00:00Z)\n  - Evan shared one of his recent works, which is a painting. (event_time: 2023-08-19T18:17:00Z)\n  - Evan took a picture at his favorite spot by the beach. (event_time: 2023-11-03T00:00:00Z)\n  - Sam commented that the photo Evan shared looks stunning. (event_time: 2023-08-13T16:09:00Z)\n  - The picture was taken at Evan's favorite spot by the beach. (event_time: 2023-11-03T00:00:00Z)\n  - Evan came across a pic while tidying up. (event_time: 2023-08-27T10:18:00Z)\n  - The vibrant colors of the photo brought a smile to Evan's face during last spring. (event_time: 2023-04-01T00:00:00Z)\n  - The photo reminds Evan of last spring. (event_time: 2024-01-11T21:37:00Z)\n  - Evan observed amazing views during a trip he took las