erience.\n  - hobbies: Jolene is seeking tips for balancing hobbies and studies; Deborah focuses on teaching yoga and organizing a yoga event last month.\n  - teaching: Deborah started teaching a neighborhood yoga class and finds it rewarding to watch it transform her neighbors.\n  - yoga event: Deborah organized a yoga event last month, which she enjoyed and found cool. Jolene later asked for details on how it was put together.\n  - yoga pals: Deborah considers her yoga pals her second family, as they have supported each other through challenges. Her mum was also a significant source of motivation and attended her yoga classes.\n  - Deb: Deborah (Deb) ran a free community gardening class yesterday with her neighbor, which was enjoyed by people of any age.\n  - meditation routine: Jolene signed up for a meditation course at a retreat near a lake; Deborah uses meditation as a routine part of life.\n  - mindfulness: Jolene realized the importance of mindfulness, self-care, and balance alongside engineering studies after a meditation retreat in Phuket. Deborah encourages this practice.\n  - things that bring you joy: Deborah advises Jolene to make time for 'things that bring you joy' to experience joy.\n  - her: Deborah cherishes memories with 'her' at a spot where they watched a beautiful sunset; Deborah also carries an amulet belonging to 'her'. Jolene adopted 'her' two years ago for company.\n  - Deborah's mother: Deborah's mother enjoyed reading and believed art could give strong emotions and uniquely connect people. Deborah feels close to her mother when visiting art shows.\n  - her memory: Deborah finds peace in keeping her mom's memory alive through art, which brings back powerful emotions and offers comfort after her loss.\n  - Exercise: Deborah started a running group with Anna for fitness. She takes them for runs in the park every morning and evening, valuing exercise and nature.\n  - Deborah's mom: Deborah's mom had a big passion for cooking and made amazing