d Audrey about her dogs' breed and what they enjoy doing most, following a discussion about dog training and finding dog-friendly spots.\n  - dog grooming course: Audrey took a dog grooming course and learned many techniques, offering to share tips with Andrew.\n  - cuatro perros: Audrey has cuatro perros (four dogs) whom she loves; she got a tattoo of them on her arm and took them all to the vet, which was chaotic.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n  - puppy: Andrew adopted a new puppy named Toby. Andrew shared photos of his puppy playing in the park, which made Andrew and Audrey happy.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - Andrew: Andrew reacted positively to Audrey's groomed pets and is preparing a space for Scout, including a bed, toys, and puppy pads, for a slow introduction to Toby and Buddy.\n  - dog owners: Audrey meets with a dog owners group once a week for tips and playdates. She considered a positive reinforcement training class workshop advertised at her pet store.\n  - Andrew (assistant): Andrew asked Audrey about the tips she received from her dogs' appointment with an animal behaviorist. Andrew suggested visiting a lake near a trail to see the autumn colors.\n  - workshop about bonding with my pet: Audrey heard about a positive reinforcement training class workshop at her local pet store and met a friendly dog there. Andrew expressed interest.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - Max: Max was Audrey's childhood dog. They took long walks where Max would sniff and mark territory. Audrey shared worries and hopes with Max, viewing him as a great listener.\n  - neighborhoods: Audrey's childhood memories include taking long walks with her dog, Max, in the neighborhood, where she shared worries and hopes with him.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - collars: Audrey obtained new, cute collars and tags for her dogs and shared a picture of them.\n  - the doggos: Audrey takes the doggos for walks in the park to relax and clear her mind, as they offer a nature environment.\n  - neighbors' dogs: Audrey organized a doggy playdate with the neighbors' dogs, and seeing them wag their tails was sweet.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2078,"context_chars":8215,"retrieval_duration":0.1752936840057373,"response_duration":3.481976270675659,"total_duration":3.6572699546813965,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer addresses the shared frustration of not being able to find pet-friendly spots, which aligns with the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides clear information about Audrey's frustration regarding dog ownership, specifically mentioning her difficulty in finding pet-friendly spots. This directly aligns with the golden answer, which states that the shared frustration for both Audrey and Andrew is not being able to find pet-friendly spots. Therefore, all necessary information to answer the question is present in the context.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Audrey finds it frustrating not to find pet-friendly spots.","Andrew expressed sympathy to Audrey regarding the search for dog-friendly spots to rent."]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_5","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_5_qa_14","category":"1","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What is something that Andrew really misses while working in the city?","golden_answer":"being in nature","hypothesis":"Andrew really misses the connection with nature while working in the city. He feels that his current job and living situation make it hard to find peace and connect with the outdoors. Specifically, he misses the peacefulness of being out on a hike and being at the beach.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Andrew feels like he is missing out on nature. (event_time: 2023-04-16T16:19:00Z)\n  - Andrew misses being at the beach. (event_time: 2023-10-04T16:18:00Z)\n  - Andrew has recently been missing the connection with nature. (event_time: 2023-06-26T13:51:00Z)\n  - Andrew's current situation (job and living location) makes it hard to connect with nature and find peace. (event_time: 2023-10-04T16:18:00Z)\n  - Andrew (assistant) misses hanging out with a dog. (event_time: 2023-04-02T14:42:00Z)\n  - Andrew misses the peacefulness of being out on a hike (event_time: 2023-04-16T16:19:00Z)\n  - City living makes it hard for Andrew to experience connection (event_time: 2023-04-16T16:19:00Z)\n  - Andrew lacks the opportunity to go outside into nature while in the city (event_time: 2023-04-16T16:19:00Z)\n  - City living makes it hard for Andrew t