fer nice, sunny days spent in the grass.\n  - sushi: Andrew tried sushi at a new spot and it was great; Audrey saw the description and decided to order sushi for dinner.\n  - a glass of wine: Audrey pours a glass of wine while cooking and eating, describing it as therapeutic self-care.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - breeds: Audrey stated she has four dogs, two Jack Russell mixes and two Chihuahua mixes. She believes some dog breeds bond better than others.\n  - snow: Audrey's dogs hate snow; they were confused when taken to a snowy park last winter and prefer sunny days.\n  - Pixie: Pixie is one of Audrey's four dogs, a Chihuahua mix, who curls up in her own bed to relax. Audrey is busy giving attention to her four dogs.\n  - bungee jumping: Andrew is inspired by rock climbing to try more outdoor activities, including kayaking and bungee jumping, as mentioned by Audrey.\n  - paws: Audrey pays attention to sensitive areas like ears and paws during gentle grooming, emphasizing patience and positivity.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - plants: Andrew mentioned getting more plants for his house; Audrey suggested plants can make a home peaceful.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - Audrey (assistant): Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist last Wednesday for her dogs who were acting abnormally and