ul feeling is good for recharging and thinking.\n  - the feeling of the sun: Jolene mentioned 'the feeling of the sun' as a small win that makes life better, something to be more mindful and grateful about.\n  - cozy nook: Jolene mentioned that a cozy nook is a must and that the beach is a great place for finding peace and relaxation.\n  - pet: Jolene has a pet that brings happiness and comfort. Deborah has cats, one named Luna, and acknowledges pets bring comfort.\n  - creature: Jolene bought a new aquarium the day before yesterday and now has a calm creature named Seraphim in it.\n  - him: Deborah told Jolene that Jolene is great for \"taming him\" and asked how Jolene got him.\n  - Susie: Jolene mentioned that Susie is a great companion. Jolene has had Susie for two years.\n  - chill: Jolene was asked by Deborah if finding 'chill' helps her find her chill or improve concentration.\n  - joy: Jolene experienced a new level of joy and happiness after a retreat in Phuket, which inspired her to incorporate relaxation and balance with her engineering studies.\n  - joy on the way: Jolene agreed to Deborah's advice to find joy on the way.\n  - positive feedback: Jolene was thrilled to receive positive feedback, finding it rewarding that her efforts were appreciated. She is currently focusing on studying and gaining more experience.\n  - comfort: Deborah found comfort in reconnecting with her mom's old friends, noting how pets also bring comfort and peace.\n  - Jolene and Anna: Deborah mentioned Anna got her a tasty vegan stir-fry (tofu, veg, ginger, soy sauce). Jolene mentioned doing yoga and meditation last Friday for me-time.\n  - video games: Jolene shared that her passion for video games started when her parents got her something related when she was 10 years old.\n  - Jolene and her partner: Jolene and her partner went scuba diving last Friday and found a cool spot to explore. Jolene also shared a picture of herself and her partner at a music festival last year.\n  