s care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - Andrew's GF: Andrew's GF, Toby, played board games with Andrew last Tuesday. Andrew's GF is mentioned in relation to a sweet sweater and possibly visiting a dog park.\n  - new pups: Andrew is looking to adopt a doggo after browsing websites, visiting shelters, and asking friends. Audrey mentioned that meeting new pups brings happiness.\n  - breed: Andrew asked Audrey about her dogs' breed and what they enjoy doing most, following a discussion about dog training and finding dog-friendly spots.\n  - doggo: Audrey groomed her dogs, who looked cute with shiny coats after being good at the salon. Andrew adopted another dog and shared a photo.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - Andrew's girlfriend: Andrew's girlfriend creates a safe and fun space for Scout, and she is encouraged to slowly introduce Scout to Toby and Buddy.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - Andrew (assistant): Andrew asked Audrey about the tips she received from her dogs' appointment with an animal behaviorist. Andrew suggested visiting a lake near a trail to see the autumn colors.\n  - cuatro perros: Audrey has cuatro perros (four dogs) whom she loves; she got a tattoo of them on her arm and took them all to the vet, which was chaotic.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n  - doggy daycare: Andrew mentioned a doggy daycare near him that has a big indoor space for dogs to play.\n  - My dogs: Au