ds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - writing projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be the best thing ever, a mix of highs and lows. Writing is an escape, a way to express feelings, and healing.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2013,"context_chars":8090,"retrieval_duration":0.1948404312133789,"response_duration":2.725529432296753,"total_duration":2.920369863510132,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions 'parts of a screenplay' which aligns with the gold answer 'screenplay bits', and it also references the same time frame of 'yesterday', making it correct.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides clear information that Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that were shown on the big screen yesterday. This directly answers the question about what Joanna wrote that appeared on the big screen, matching the golden answer of 'screenplay bits'. All necessary details are present, including the specific reference to the screenplay and the timing of the event.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay","the screenplay was shown on the big screen yesterday"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_5","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_5_qa_37","category":"2","difficulty":"unknown","query":"When did Audrey get into an accident in the park?","golden_answer":"between October 19 and 24, 2023","hypothesis":"Audrey had an accident while playing with her pups at the park on October 17, 2023.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memo