egies used.\n  - hobbies and studies: Deborah finds time management and scheduling helpful for balancing hobbies and studies, which Jolene also inquired about.\n  - daily schedule: Deborah creates a daily schedule or to-do list to manage time and stay organized with projects and deadlines.\n  - planner: Deborah suggested using planners or schedulers for time management to ensure time for oneself.\n  - study plan: Deborah suggested using planners or schedulers for time management and offered help with a study plan.\n  - schedule: Jolene plans to check her schedule next month to arrange a time to chat with Deborah.\n  - studying: Jolene has a schedule that includes studying, classes, and personal time, using yoga and meditation for balance.\n  - time management: Jolene struggles with balancing engineering, relationship, and personal growth, and is now using a bullet journal for time management.\n  - planners: Jolene started using a bullet journal to track tasks and stay organized as part of her time management strategies.\n  - routines: Jolene is seeking new routines. Deborah suggested a gentle yoga flow focused on breathing and grounding to help Jolene cope, and offered to send a tutorial video.\n  - Jolene and Anna: Deborah mentioned Anna got her a tasty vegan stir-fry (tofu, veg, ginger, soy sauce). Jolene mentioned doing yoga and meditation last Friday for me-time.\n  - organization: No specific organization was mentioned in the conversation between Jolene and Deborah, which focused on stress, exams, deadlines, and time management.\n  - deadlines: Deborah expressed concern to Jolene about her exams and deadlines, noting the situation is difficult. Jolene confirmed it is tough, stressful, and requires her to constantly play catch-up.\n  - peaceful time: Deborah experienced nostalgia and longing at a meaningful place, bringing flowers. Jolene mentioned a calm and peaceful feeling is good for recharging and thinking.\n  - routine: Jolene finds having a routine helpfu