 for the community yesterday, which was well-attended by people of all ages.\n  - Deborah's dad: Deborah's dad passed away suddenly two days ago. Deborah is channeling grief by spending time with family and looking at memories, including her parents' 1993 wedding photos.\n  - places visited: Jolene visited Rio de Janeiro, checked out yoga classes, and explored cafes. Deborah visited her mom's house, which is important to her.\n  - Deb: Deborah (Deb) ran a free community gardening class yesterday with her neighbor, which was enjoyed by people of any age.\n  - beauties: Jolene encourages Deborah to keep finding 'beauties', following a conversation about music festivals and a yoga retreat.\n  - being outside: Jolene likes being outside because it is calming and refreshing, and asked Deborah if she has any special spots she likes to go to.\n  - Deborah's parents: Deborah's parents got married in 1993, as seen in a family wedding photo.\n  - stories about Deborah's mom: Deborah reconnected with her mom's old friends, and hearing stories about her mom was emotional, bringing a mix of happy and sad feelings, but overall comforting.\n  - last summer: Karlie and Deborah had a great time hiking last summer, which is when their last photo was taken.\n  - Deborah's mum: Deborah's mum was her biggest fan and source of motivation, often attending Deborah's yoga classes with her.\n  - friend: Deborah misses a friend who sent her a supportive quote: \"Let go of what no longer serves you.\" Previous summary mentioned she lost a friend.\n  - yoga retreat: Jolene attended an awesome yoga retreat described as peaceful with amazing sunrise views, making attendees feel alive and grateful. Deborah inquires about a future experience.\n  - her presence: Deborah feels her mother's presence when sitting in a specific place, which comforts her during difficult times following her father's death.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2011,"context_chars":8149,"retrieval_duration":0.24480271339416504