l video.\n  - setback with Jolene's project: Jolene experienced a huge setback with her project last week, causing her to lose all her work, which was frustrating and depressing. Deborah offered support.\n  - efforts: Deborah encouraged Jolene that her efforts will bear fruit and advised her not to give up.\n  - internship: Jolene is considering more internships to further enhance her skills after receiving positive feedback on her efforts, building on past experiences like a hectic internship.\n  - work files: Jolene lost her work files, which caused stress, but meditation helped her regain clarity.\n  - Green tech: Jolene wants to look into Green tech to see how she can contribute and suggested a volunteer program where engineers teach STEM to underprivileged kids.\n  - deadlines: Deborah expressed concern to Jolene about her exams and deadlines, noting the situation is difficult. Jolene confirmed it is tough, stressful, and requires her to constantly play catch-up.\n  - project: Deborah started a community cleanup project for fundraising. Jolene had a setback with her own project, losing all work, and Deborah supports her ambition.\n  - great things: Deborah told Jolene that she is sure great things will keep coming her way and encouraged her to keep up the good work and follow her passions.\n  - someone close to Jolene: Someone close to Jolene used to bake cookies with her.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2010,"context_chars":8312,"retrieval_duration":0.18959712982177734,"response_duration":2.6555776596069336,"total_duration":2.845174789428711,"grade":false,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer states that Jolene worked on the project for 3 months and 5 days, which does not match the gold answer of four months.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all necessary information to answer the question about how long Jolene worked on the robotics project. It states that Jolene was assigned the project on February 1, 2023, and that she finished it last month, which is May 2023. This indicates that she worked on the project for four months, aligning perfectly with the golden answer.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["Jolene was assigned the robotics project on February 1, 2023","Jolene finished the project last month (May 2023)"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_8","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_8_qa_15","category":"1","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What kind of unhealthy snacks does Sam enjoy eating?","golden_answer":"soda, candy","hypothesis":"Sam enjoys eating sugary snacks and soda, as he has admitted to struggling with cravings for these unhealthy options. He finds sugary treats tempting and has purchased unhealthy snacks recently, which has led to feelings of guilt.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Sam admitted that he could not resist unhealthy snacks. (event_time: 2023-10-14T16:07:00Z)\n  - Sam purchased unhealthy snacks during the past week. (event_time: 2023-10-14T16:07:00Z)\n  - Sam finds sugary treats tempting. (event_time: 2023-09-11T09:28:00Z)\n  - Sam is struggling with occasional cravings for sugary drinks and snacks. (event_time: 2023-09-11T09:28:00Z)\n  - Sam stated he needs to do better regarding unhealthy snacks. (event_time: 2023-10-14T16:07:00Z)\n  - Sam currently continues to consume soda, which Sam knows is not the best habit. (event_time: 2023-06-06T15:55:00Z)\n  - Sam considers the consumption of soda to be not the best habit. (event_time: 2023-06-06T15:5